  "notes": "Fresh process per cell; Escape, the arm keys and the drop key are real key taps over the viewport; readback after the gesture (constraint on/off + settings, element selection, tool pipe). Neutral copy for the vibe3d-only witness tests/test_constraint_boot.d; the pen-placement cells live with the pen tests."
 },
 "rig": {
  "scene": "boot mesh holds a 64x32 sphere r=1 centre (0,1,0) built by geometry edits (no tool armed, no pipe write) and becomes the BACKGROUND layer; a new empty FOREGROUND mesh is created and one triangle is committed into it; top view",
  "post_first_drop": "cells marked post_first_drop=true arm the move tool and drop it (two key taps) before any other setup"
 },
 "law": {
  "boot": "at a fresh boot the background constraint is DISABLED (absent from the pipe). It becomes enabled with geometry off, offset 0, handle on, double-sided off at the FIRST tool drop of the session (drop key or the Escape that drops an armed tool; any tool). Arming a tool does not add it. Once removed it is NOT re-added by later drops, nor by a new scene. A new scene keeps an enabled constraint.",
  "escape": "with no tool armed, an ENABLED constraint is a held task whatever its settings (default, geometry point, or handle off): Escape removes it (disables it) and keeps the element selection; the next Escape drops the selection. A disabled constraint holds nothing: Escape drops the selection.",
  "tool_switch": "arming another tool, dropping it and arming the pen keep a non-default geometry setting (point stays point).",
  "panel": "while enabled, the tool-properties panel shows the full constraint block (offset, handle, double sided, geometry) with no tool armed and with the move tool; while disabled the panel shows no constraint rows."
 },
 "law_remembered": {
  "remembered_constraint": "the editor remembers the last constraint the user turned on (fresh prefs remember the background constraint with geometry off, offset 0, handle on, double-sided off). Every tool DROP re-inserts the remembered constraint. Turning the constraint off by its own toggle, or the Escape that clears it, forgets it; turning it on by its own toggle remembers it again (the next drop re-inserts it).",
  "what_is_a_drop": "the drop key, the Escape that drops an armed tool, and a NEW SCENE while a tool is armed (the new scene drops the tool first). A tool SWITCH (arming another tool while one is armed) is NOT a drop and inserts nothing; arming from no tool inserts nothing.",
  "toggle_on_fields": "turning the constraint on by its own toggle uses the remembered field values: at a fresh boot geometry off, offset 0, handle on, double-sided off; a value the user set earlier in the session (geometry point) survives toggle off + toggle on",
  "new_scene": "a new scene keeps every tool-pipe stage and its values (falloff type + values, action centre, an enabled constraint) and keeps symmetry; with no tool armed it inserts nothing; with a tool armed it drops it (see what_is_a_drop)"
 },
